# Every text file in Murmur is LF in the repository, and LF in the working tree.
#
# This exists because a whitespace flip can hide the change it rides with: a Windows editor
# re-saving a file as CRLF turns a 40 line edit into a 13,000 line diff, which is a review that
# cannot be read. Nothing here is a style preference.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` is what makes a Windows editor's
# CRLF save normalise on the way in rather than landing in a commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never inspects or converts them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.wav  binary
*.aiff binary
*.vst3 binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.onnx binary
